# Fixerrors Workflow

- Run `npm run fixerrors` for the registered v4 path: repeatable-read snapshot of **active** `error_logs`, local analysis artifacts, same-process archive of those exact IDs, then 12-month retention of expired archived rows. `--no-clear` is rejected before any database connection.
- Trusted mutation is only `fixerrors-exact-snapshot-v4` (see `.cursor/commands/fixerrors.md` and `scripts/automation/trusted-operational-actions.ts`). Archive updates `status`/`archived_at`. Retention deletes only expired archived rows bound to a captured candidate set. Never reconstruct or loosen archive/retention arguments.
- After a non-empty snapshot, follow the command: one premium analysis Task writes `docs_private/error-analysis-decision.md`; implement only `fix` clusters; one CRITICAL cluster must not escalate unrelated FAST/STANDARD clusters.
- Read `docs_private/error-analysis.md`, `docs_private/error-analysis-decision.md` when present, `docs_private/error-fix-log.md` when it exists, plus generated automation review/follow-up files and `docs_private/error-snapshot.json` / `docs_private/error-snapshots/`.
- Summarize actionable error groups without reproducing sensitive payloads, tokens, user data, or full stack traces.
- Claim remote errors were archived only when the automation run log explicitly records a successful trusted archive step.
- Treat `failed` / `indeterminate` archive or retention outcomes as manual-investigation states; do not auto-retry.
- Debug UI clear and `scripts/clear-all-error-logs.ts` remain untrusted unbounded archive-active surfaces (`R-DEBUG-CLEAR-UNTRUSTED`).
- Keep every generated error and automation artifact local and ignored.
- Leftover v1 snapshots and the 2026-08-11 analysis report are not cleanup sources.
